# Routing isolation

Navigation belongs in `src/routes/**`, not in pages, components, or hooks.

- Use `useNavigate`, `navigate()`, `redirect()`, `Link`, and `Outlet` only in `src/routes/**`.
- `src/router.ts` only assembles the route tree.
- Pages and components receive typed callbacks (`onHomeClick`, `onSuccess`) and route-derived props.
- Do not import `@tanstack/react-router` outside `src/routes/`, `src/router.ts`, and `src/main.tsx`.
- ESLint and `src/architecture.test.ts` enforce this — add a callback instead of disabling rules.

```tsx
// BAD — page navigates
function LoginPage() {
  const navigate = useNavigate()
  // ...
}

// GOOD — route owns navigation
function LoginRoute() {
  const navigate = useNavigate()
  return <LoginPage onSuccess={() => navigate({ to: '/' })} />
}
```
